{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"After corrected semantic scoring, the core result is stable: 261 questions had stable-correct beliefs, and 212 (81.2%, 95% Wilson CI 76.0–85.5%) became false under incentive. The decisive detector result is negative: on the same-pressure false-vs-false contrast, the lie probe is at chance (AUROC 0.481, 95% bootstrap CI 0.415–0.544), while it strongly separates pressured lies from pressured correct answers (0.975). That pattern is consistent with detecting false output features, not the belief–report mismatch itself."}}
