{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"Research execution is complete. The full study, real-model outputs, probes, statistical analysis, figures, and reproducibility checks are available in the workspace.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct gave stable-correct neutral answers on 261/500 questions.\n- Under incentive, 212/261 became false: 81.2% yield (95% CI 76.0–85.5%).\n- Operational lies comprised 31.9% of 664 false reports.\n- The lie probe appeared strong when prompts differed (AUROC 0.985), but prompt tokens alone achieved 1.000.\n- With pressure and falsity controlled, the lie probe was at chance distinguishing lies from unknown-state false outputs: AUROC 0.478 [0.414, 0.538].\n- Both lie and hallucination probes strongly distinguished false from correct pressured answers, suggesting sensitivity to falsehood/recall rather than lying specifically.\n- Two complete reruns produced byte-identical raw outputs and activation archives.\n\nPrimary deliverables:\n\n- [Full research report](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/REPORT.md)\n- [Project overview and reproduction instructions](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/README.md)\n- [Experimental plan](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/planning.md)\n- [Experiment implementation](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/src/run_experiment.py)\n- [Statistical analysis](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/src/analyze_results.py)\n- [Detector metrics](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/results/processed/detector_metrics.csv)\n- [Mechanism shares](/workspaces/detect-different-lies-ce22-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/results/processed/mechanism_shares.csv)\n\nThe literature-review, critical-analysis, and data-analysis workflows shaped the evidence positioning, validity audit, statistical controls, and deliberately cautious conclusions."}}
